 for bestpractices and # Internal Module/Template Builder

## Overview
Design and implement a modular, multi-tenant Internal Module/Template Builder that enables admins and builders to define tenant-specific mini-apps (modules) with rich metadata, UI entry points, data binding schemas, versioned deployments, and fine-grained permissions. The system includes a Template Marketplace/Registry, live previews using shared UI patterns, and robust role-based access control. It must support three primary pages: Create/Add Module, Internal Modules Hub, and Edit/Manage Module, with clear versioning, deployment, and departmental assignment capabilities.

This prompt enforces runtime safety rules (null/undefined guards for arrays, proper use of data ?? [], correct useState initialization, and explicit validation) and adheres to a dependency-first implementation order: auth/data setup and core data scaffolding must be completed before UI/dashboard features.

---

## Components to Build

- Create / Add Module Page (page_create_module_028)
  - Builder interface for creating new internal modules (mini-apps)
  - Metadata fields: module name, description, tenant scoping, version metadata, tags
  - Data bindings: define data schema bindings to unified context (e.g., ModuleContext, ModuleRecord)
  - UI entry: specify route or UI entry component for the module (live preview)
  - Permissions mapping: role-based access definitions (which roles can view/use)
  - Validation and live preview: ensure schema and permissions pass client-side validation
  - Version and deployment hooks: initial version creation and readiness flags

- Internal Modules Hub (page_internal_modules_015)
  - Registry and management surface for tenant-specific modules
  - Install/installers: import/install modules from marketplace or templates
  - Configuration: per-module settings (data bindings, UI entry, theming overrides)
  - Permissions assignment UI: map module-level permissions to roles/departments
  - Status indicators: installed, version, last deployed, health, dependencies
  - Searching, filtering, sorting, and bulk actions (disable, uninstall, rollback)
  - Live preview / test harness per module

- Edit / Manage Module Page (page_edit_module_029)
  - Module editing interface for existing modules
  - View versions: list with timestamps, change details
  - Rollback: revert to previous version with approval guard
  - Assignment tooling: assign module to departments, update role permissions
  - Conflict resolution: handle data-binding changes, migration prompts
  - Audit trail: capture edits, version changes, and deployment actions

- Shared Core Backbone
  - Data models for Module, Version, PermissionSet, DepartmentBinding, Tenant
  - Marketplace/Template module registry
  - Live Preview Engine: render a sandboxed iframe or isolated component using the module’s UI entry
  - Access control layer: RBAC integration with existing auth subsystem
  - API layer scaffolding for create/read/update/delete, install, rollback, versioning
  - Validation framework for input data, schema bindings, and permissions

---

## Implementation Requirements

### Frontend

- UI Framework and Style
  - Use the project’s design system and visual language (dark, high-contrast enterprise aesthetic).
  - Reusable React components with strong type hints (TypeScript recommended).
  - 12-column responsive grid; hero sections with left/right balance where applicable.
  - Card-based UI for module tiles, metadata panels, and settings.
  - Accessible controls (ARIA labels, keyboard navigability, focus rings).

- Pages and Components
  - CreateModulePanel
    - Form fields: Module Name, Description, Tenant Scope (multi-select), Version (auto-generated), Tags
    - Data Binding Builder: UI to define module data bindings to Unified Context, with live validation
    - UI Entry Selector: select or upload a UI entry component or route
    - Permissions Builder: map roles to allowed actions within module (View/Edit/Use/DataRead/DataWrite)
    - Live Preview Pane: render a sandbox preview of the module using the selected UI entry
  - ModulesHub
    - ModuleGrid: tiles showing name, version, status, bindings summary
    - Install/Configure/Uninstall actions per module
    - Permission Mapper per module (assign roles to actions)
    - Search/Filter: by name, tags, tenant, status, bindings
    - Version/Deployment status badges and quick rollback access
  - EditModulePanel
    - Version History: chronological list with diff summary
    - Rollback Control: revert to chosen version with confirmation
    - Edit fields: name, description, bindings, UI entry, permissions
    - Department Assignment: add/remove departments; show impact notes
    - Migration Planner: warn on breaking data-binding changes
  - LivePreviewEngine
    - Secure sandbox to render module UI entry with mock data
    - Passes a minimal context to module (tenant, user role, department)
    - Sandbox should prevent cross-module data leakage
  - API Integration (frontend)
    - Consistent typing for responses; guard against nulls
    - Use data ?? [] for list results; Array.isArray guards for mappings
    - Initialize useState with [] for array-based state
    - Validation on submit: required fields, unique module name, valid bindings

- Runtime Safety (CRITICAL)
  - All lists from API must be treated as data ?? []
  - Guard all array method calls: (items ?? []).map(...) or Array.isArray(items) ? items.map(...) : []
  - useState<Type[]>([]) initialization
  - API response shapes validated: const list = Array.isArray(response?.data) ? response.data : []
  - Optional chaining usage for nested API responses: obj?.property?.nested
  - Destructuring with defaults: const { items = [], count = 0 } = response ?? {}

### Backend

- Data Models
  - Tenant, Module, ModuleVersion, DepartmentBinding, Role, PermissionSet, DataBinding
  - Module
    - id, tenantId, name, description, createdAt, updatedAt
    - uiEntry (string: route or component key), dataBindings: DataBinding[], permissions: PermissionSet
    - status: Draft | Published | Deprecated | Archived
    - versions: ModuleVersion[]
  - ModuleVersion
    - id, moduleId, versionTag, changelog, createdAt, isActive
    - migrationNotes, bindingDiff
  - DataBinding
    - bindingName, sourceContext, targetEntity, fieldMappings
  - PermissionSet
    - roleId, actions[], scope (module-level permissions)
  - DepartmentBinding
    - departmentId, moduleId, accessLevel
  - MarketplaceTemplate
    - templateId, name, description, bindingsTemplate, previewUI

- API Endpoints (REST-ish or GraphQL)
  - Auth-required
  - GET /tenants/{tenantId}/modules
  - POST /tenants/{tenantId}/modules
  - GET /tenants/{tenantId}/modules/{moduleId}
  - PUT /tenants/{tenantId}/modules/{moduleId}
  - DELETE /tenants/{tenantId}/modules/{moduleId}
  - POST /tenants/{tenantId}/modules/{moduleId}/versions
  - POST /tenants/{tenantId}/modules/{moduleId}/rollback
  - POST /tenants/{tenantId}/modules/{moduleId}/install (from marketplace)
  - POST /tenants/{tenantId}/modules/{moduleId}/deploy
  - GET /tenants/{tenantId}/modules/{moduleId}/versions
  - GET /templates (Marketplace)
  - POST /templates/install (purchase or install from marketplace)
  - GET /tenants/{tenantId}/modules/{moduleId}/permissions
  - PUT /tenants/{tenantId}/modules/{moduleId}/permissions

- Data Mersistence & Migrations
  - Ensure tenant isolation on all module data
  - Validate binding schemas and enforce invariants on write
  - Versioning: keep history with non-destructive migrations where possible
  - Rollback: implement safe rollback with migration plan and user confirmation

- Security & Validation
  - RBAC: define permissions for Module CRUD, install, configure, deploy, rollback
  - Validate data bindings against the unified data model (type checks, required fields)
  - Protect live preview sandbox with strict origin checks and no cross-tenant leaks
  - Audit logs for create/update/delete/version deployments

### Integration

- Shared UI Patterns
  - Reuse existing pattern for live previews, forms, and list views
  - Consistent theming, typography, and spacing with global design tokens
- Data Synchronization
  - Module bindings reference Unified Data Layer; ensure data context compatibility
  - When a module is bound to a data source, ensure data source permissions align with role permissions
- Marketplace Registry
  - Template marketplace to browse, install, and instantiate modules
  - Preview templates, dependencies, and version compatibility checks
- Live Preview
  - Sandbox feed passes: tenantId, userRole, departments, and module-specific mock data
  - Preview should reflect binding mappings and UI entry points

---

## User Experience Flow

1) Admin lands on Internal Modules Hub
- Sees a grid/list of modules with status, version, bindings summary
- Can filter by tenant, status, tag, binding
- Clicks “Create Module” to start

2) Create / Add Module
- Fills Module Name, Description
- Selects Tenant Scope (multi-tenant aware or single-tenant)
- Builds Data Bindings via a UI schema builder (select source context, map fields)
- Chooses or defines UI Entry (route or component key) for module entry
- Configures Permissions (roles mapped to actions)
- Uses Live Preview to see how the module would render
- Submits to create initial Module with Version 1.0
- Redirects to Module Details or Hub with new entry

3) Install/Configure Module (Hub)
- Admin can Install a module from Marketplace or configure existing
- Adjust per-module settings: data bindings, UI entry overrides, theming
- Assign department access and role-based permissions
- Deploy initial version if ready; view deployment health

4) Edit / Manage Module
- Open module to edit: change metadata, bindings, UI entry, permissions
- View Version History: compare, choose to rollback
- Rollback to a previous version with confirmation and migration plan
- Re-assign module to departments; adjust access as needed
- Save changes; publish new version; audit logs recorded

5) Live Preview
- At any time, preview renders within a sandbox
- Changes to bindings, UI entry, or permissions update the live preview instantly or on save
- Preview reflects tenant context and the current user’s role

6) Administration & Governance
- Admin reviews installation status, dependencies, and module health
- Logs actions (creation, update, deployment, rollback) for audit

---

## Build Order & Dependencies (Mandatory)

- Prerequisites
  - Auth & RBAC system in place (roles, permissions, session management)
  - Core data layer with Tenant, User, Department models
  - Unified Data & Context Layer established (for data bindings)
  - Marketplace/Template registry scaffold deployed

- Blocks
  - Block 1: Module data model and API scaffold
  - Block 2: Permission mapping and RBAC integration for module actions
  - Block 3: Live Preview sandbox engine
  - Block 4: UI components for Create/Hub/Edit pages
  - Block 5: Versioning, rollback, and deployment workflows
  - Block 6: Marketplace integration and template consumption

- Sequencing Rule
  - Auth/access control and core data setup must be completed before dashboard/workspace/analytics pages when both exist

---

## Technical Specifications

- Data Models (TypeScript or ORM definitions)
  - Tenant { id, name, ... }
  - Module { id, tenantId, name, description, uiEntry, status, createdAt, updatedAt, versions: ModuleVersion[], bindings: DataBinding[], permissions: PermissionSet[], departments: DepartmentBinding[] }
  - ModuleVersion { id, moduleId, versionTag, changelog, createdAt, isActive, bindingDiff }
  - DataBinding { bindingName, sourceContext, targetEntity, fieldMappings: Record<string, string> }
  - PermissionSet { roleId: string, actions: string[], scope: string } // per module
  - DepartmentBinding { departmentId, accessLevel }
  - MarketplaceTemplate { id, name, description, previewUI, bindingsTemplate, dependencies }

- API Endpoints
  - REST structure as outlined in Backend section
  - Input validation and error handling
  - Consistent response shapes with data ?? [] fallbacks on arrays

- Security
  - JWT/OAuth session, RBAC checks on each endpoint
  - Tenant-scoped access control
  - Sandbox isolation for live previews

- Validation
  - Server-side and client-side validation for required fields
  - Binding schemas must conform to unified data model
  - Unique module name per tenant

---

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Modules can be created with valid metadata, data bindings, UI entry, and permission mappings
- [ ] Live Preview renders module UI entry with mock data and respects binding mappings
- [ ] Modules Hub lists modules with accurate status, versions, and binding summaries; install/configure/uninstall works
- [ ] Edit Module allows version history access, rollback, and updates to metadata, bindings, UI entry, and permissions
- [ ] Rollback to previous version preserves data integrity and provides an migration plan
- [ ] Data access is tenant-isolated; RBAC correctly restricts module actions by role
- [ ] All arrays and API results guarded with null/undefined safety patterns (data ?? [], Array.isArray checks)
- [ ] useState initializations for array data are [] (e.g., useState<Module[]>([]))
- [ ] Validation errors surface clearly in the UI, with inline hints

---

## UI/UX Guidelines

Apply the project’s design system consistently across all pages.

- Visual Style
  - Adhere to the specified color palette and typography
  - High-contrast surfaces with subtle borders and glow effects
  - Card-based layouts with rounded corners and soft shadows
  - Hover states with gentle elevation and border emphasis
- Layout
  - 12-column grid with responsive breakpoints
  - Clear left-aligned text blocks in hero areas; balanced right-hand preview panels
  - Generous white space; logical sectioning with accordions where appropriate
- Accessibility
  - Keyboard navigable forms and controls
  - Proper ARIA attributes for dynamic sections
  - Adequate color contrast ratios

---

## Visual Style Summary (Optional Reference Keys)

- Background: #05060A
- Center glow: #071228 → #0B1A2A
- Surface: #0F1720
- Inputs: #0C1116
- Primary accent: #9AD0FF
- Outline: #154E78
- Live indicator: #00D27A
- Text: #F7FAFF (primary), #8FA0B0 (secondary)
- Borders: rgba(255,255,255,0.03)
- Button: #FFFFFF (fill)

---

## Notes on Coding Practices

- Enforce the runtime safety rules explicitly in all code:
  - Use data ?? [] wherever API results are consumed for arrays
  - Guard array method calls: (items ?? []).map(...) or Array.isArray(items) ? items.map(...) : []
  - Initialize array state with useState<Type[]>([])
  - Validate API shapes: const list = Array.isArray(response?.data) ? response.data : []
  - Optional chaining for nested API results: obj?.property?.nested
  - Destructuring with defaults: const { items = [], count = 0 } = response ?? {}

